  "notes": "Emphasizes completeness — reading every part of a text without skipping. Often used when describing a thorough or disciplined approach to reading.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {一気|いっき}に{通読|つうどく}する — to read through in one sitting\n- {全巻|ぜんかん}{通読|つうどく} — reading through all volumes\n- {通読|つうどく}に{値|あたい}する — worth reading through\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {精読|せいどく} — close reading, careful reading (focuses on depth of comprehension)\n- {速読|そくどく} — speed reading (focuses on reading quickly)\n- {多読|たどく} — extensive reading (reading large quantities)\n- {拾|ひろ}い{読|よ}み — selective reading, reading bits and pieces (the opposite approach)",
